# QuickNotes System Design

QuickNotes is a note-management application designed to demonstrate
front-end API integration and the architecture of a scalable online
service.

This project combines a working browser-based API client with
backend design documentation for a service intended to support
one million registered users.

## Project objectives

- Retrieve notes from an API using GET.
- Create notes using POST.
- Delete notes using DELETE.
- Validate user input and handle HTTP errors.
- Design a RESTful API for a production note-management service.
- Model relational data using SQL.
- Estimate system capacity and document a scalable architecture.

## Technology stack

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Vanilla JavaScript
- Fetch API
- JSONPlaceholder practice API
- PostgreSQL for the proposed production backend
- Mermaid for the architecture diagram
- Git and GitHub for version control

